      "ReverseUsernum.java": "class ReverseUsernum\n{\npublic static void main(String args [])\n{\n \nint rev=0;\nint z;\nwhile(true)\n{\nSystem.out.println(\"enter the num\");\nint x1=new java.util.Scanner(System.in).nextInt();\nint n=x1;\nwhile(x1>0)\n{\nz=x1%10;\nx1=x1/10;\n// rev=rev*10+z;\nrev=rev*10+z;\n}\n\nSystem.out.println(rev);\nif(rev==n)\nrev=0;\n\nSystem.out.println(\"do you want to continue press 1 for yes 0 for no\");\nint x2=new java.util.Scanner(System.in).nextInt();\nif(x2==1)\ncontinue;\nelse\nbreak;\n}\n}\n}",
      "SortwithOutsort.java": "class SortwithOutsort {\n// no built-in class ..import..\n    static void sort(int x[]) {\n\n        int temp;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c x.length - 1; i++) {\n            for (int j = i + 1; j \u003c x.length; j++) {\n\n                if (x[i] > x[j]) {\n                    temp = x[i];\n                    x[i] = x[j];\n                    x[j] = temp;\n                }\n\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n\n        int arr[] = {25, 10, 89, 45, 67, 99, 12};\n\n        sort(arr);\n\n        System.out.println(\"Sorted Array:\");\n\n        for (int i = 0; i \u003c arr.length; i++) {\n            System.out.print(arr[i] + \" \");\n        }\n    }\n}",
